Q: Why is my a:hover CSS working differently in Firefox? A: <p>It's because <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> tags (anchor tags) have a default <code>display</code> property of <code>inline</code></p>
<p>Due to the <strong><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/box_model" rel="nofollow noreferrer">CSS Box Model</a>,</strong> you would need to adjust your <code>padding</code>, and set the anchor tags <code>display</code> property to <code>display:block;</code></p>
<p>The <code>display:block;</code> allows the anchor tag to fill the whole space of the <code>&lt;li&gt;</code> tag. Making it a block-level element.</p>
<p>So change <strong><code>ul#top-menu li a</code></strong> to this:</p>
<pre><code>ul#top-menu li a{
    color: #FFFFFF;        
    font-size: 11pt;
    font-weight: bold;

    display: block; /* add this */
    padding: 0 10px; /* add this */
}
</code></pre>
<p>the CSS Box Model adds the content + padding + border + margin</p>
<p><a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/box_model" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Introduction to the CSS box model</a><br />
<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Display/Visual_formatting_model" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Visual formatting model</a><br />
<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Block-level_content" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Block-level content</a></p>
